        ecrm:P91_has_unit   "cm" .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/bccc74e5-5072-310f-b0a1-5f5ecc33e0eb>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Christening blanket of woven silk. Woven in white and tan with a proto-bizarre pattern. Lined with plain white silk. Attached to one corner is a label inscribed 'Christening Mantle used for 22 Spencers about 1750'.\n\nThere are three repeats in the width of the silk. Tabby ground with two wefts (white and tan) which alternate as required by the pattern. The pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a proportion of the warp threads (every fourth thread). There is no separate ground weft and no separate binding warp. The selvage is plain tabby and with several thicker outer cords."@en , "Christening blanket of woven silk, France, 1685-1695"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/d44959e8-ef41-383f-aff7-f9f96d6dac51> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Christening blanket of woven silk. Woven in white and tan with a proto-bizarre pattern. Lined with plain white silk. Attached to one corner is a label inscribed 'Christening Mantle used for 22 Spencers about 1750'.\n\nThere are three repeats in the width of the silk. Tabby ground with two wefts (white and tan) which alternate as required by the pattern. The pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a proportion of the warp threads (every fourth thread). There is no separate ground weft and no separate binding warp. The selvage is plain tabby and with several thicker outer cords."@en , "Christening blanket of woven silk, France, 1685-1695"@en ;
